{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_715fb9ad1edf43c0d8d28ba845fe2676524fcbc65931064e40126a78e9c65d0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run tests with npm test or node --test tests/unit/health.test.js, and health response format changes must update the health-check workflow and unit tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77d63c1ab4b4aa645f961b401271c5a7bb070a15b626c36369ba9e8a2e382332"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The health endpoint returns status, version, timestamp, uptime, memory usage, per-service configuration status (julesApi, database, github), and circuit breaker failure count and open state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4f6a455b967b13ab2252b5a677200b747a8824c9b26beeb9767d03ab8de7e78"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The server exposes HTTP endpoints including GET /health, GET /, GET /mcp/tools, POST /mcp/execute, GET /api/sessions/active, and GET /api/sessions/stats."},{"claim_ids":["clm_efdb0b5dedcafb5eff54d38579420f5fc55fa29ee738a9ca84ef897c30323f91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"POST /mcp/execute accepts a JSON body containing a tool name and a params object, and returns a tool-specific response based on the executed tool."}],"claim_ids":["clm_715fb9ad1edf43c0d8d28ba845fe2676524fcbc65931064e40126a78e9c65d0d","clm_77d63c1ab4b4aa645f961b401271c5a7bb070a15b626c36369ba9e8a2e382332","clm_a4f6a455b967b13ab2252b5a677200b747a8824c9b26beeb9767d03ab8de7e78","clm_efdb0b5dedcafb5eff54d38579420f5fc55fa29ee738a9ca84ef897c30323f91"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577","id":"pg_061ece61ebc55daea6a1bee0c9ed04b0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/scarmonit-antigravity-jules-orchestration-docs-api-api-reference-md-49-bee0c9ed04b0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f7f3db8b26a8591d8d4a0db9e093bc76"],"title":"Scarmonit/antigravity-jules-orchestration/docs/api/API_REFERENCE.md @ 49d26f81817c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1cdd45190120cbf2a3ff4d6309cc88e94372128423b30d05ce24329b933e7494"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A suggested-tasks scanner scans codebases for TODO/FIXME/HACK comments, ranks tasks by priority, and can create Jules sessions to fix the suggested tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c4e7be1ee8e97ba0af7c29c1c2940c46b423b5c77ed5ea5eea071e22859f435"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system is a Node.js-based custom MCP server using Streamable HTTP transport, with Joi schemas for runtime input validation and a stateless architecture for compatibility with multiple MCP clients."},{"claim_ids":["clm_715fb9ad1edf43c0d8d28ba845fe2676524fcbc65931064e40126a78e9c65d0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run tests with npm test or node --test tests/unit/health.test.js, and health response format changes must update the health-check workflow and unit tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8c4a55ec3784cc54dfbeffbe00509a7eec07496e51edf292bb24146706644b2d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Render auto-fix integration detects and fixes build failures on Jules PRs via a Render webhook receiver, build-log error pattern recognition, and AES-256-GCM encrypted credential storage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_948d25bbf066c790401bab2314a18f1ef8ca0c4488128638ee4b6fe11ad434fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A semantic memory integration provides 8 MCP tools for persistent AI memory, with SSRF protection via a domain whitelist and error message sanitization."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b54e50506debdcb18c1dae410d1869b561d8e59c1e0041118036df519d8cd68c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation appears internally inconsistent on tool count: the README states 65 MCP tools while the slash-commands doc says the commands leverage 30 MCP tools available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cad9bdc38464d4a52476acba06a3749b5f3d27181985d551193ddf7dd3decc67"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README catalogs 65 MCP tools across groups including Jules core (7), session management (5), batch processing (7), semantic memory (8), Render integration (12), Ollama LLM (4), and RAG (4)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cdb9af4fa01d31bb345f4744741db083dd0c425c4ffc9bc8e19ce5e499cc8b5e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented autonomous loop runs: user task initiation, Antigravity planning, Jules session creation via MCP, parallel execution, progress monitoring, approval gates, then merge/test completion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dd0472d4309cc1e5e4b0aba939fff98be6dd546e615c6353daf88b0c6a886693"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration variables include PORT (default 3323), required JULES_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN, DATABASE_URL, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, LOG_LEVEL, ALLOWED_ORIGINS, and SEMANTIC_MEMORY_URL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e62a5af5978ddf0dee8470c975f6519c6e21452182242f05cf52bbc2e2e72261"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Performance features include an LRU cache (100 items, 10s default TTL), a circuit breaker tripping after 5 consecutive failures with 60s reset, and retry logic with 3 exponential-backoff retries plus jitter."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ffe6810f4f16b959c6fc8727d30c44136ba5c18fe70b18c44016c41353b03b30"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites are Node.js v18+, Google Antigravity installed, a Jules API account with key, and a GitHub account with connected repositories; setup uses npm install and npm run dev."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1cdd45190120cbf2a3ff4d6309cc88e94372128423b30d05ce24329b933e7494","clm_6c4e7be1ee8e97ba0af7c29c1c2940c46b423b5c77ed5ea5eea071e22859f435","clm_715fb9ad1edf43c0d8d28ba845fe2676524fcbc65931064e40126a78e9c65d0d","clm_8c4a55ec3784cc54dfbeffbe00509a7eec07496e51edf292bb24146706644b2d","clm_948d25bbf066c790401bab2314a18f1ef8ca0c4488128638ee4b6fe11ad434fc","clm_b54e50506debdcb18c1dae410d1869b561d8e59c1e0041118036df519d8cd68c","clm_cad9bdc38464d4a52476acba06a3749b5f3d27181985d551193ddf7dd3decc67","clm_cdb9af4fa01d31bb345f4744741db083dd0c425c4ffc9bc8e19ce5e499cc8b5e","clm_dd0472d4309cc1e5e4b0aba939fff98be6dd546e615c6353daf88b0c6a886693","clm_e62a5af5978ddf0dee8470c975f6519c6e21452182242f05cf52bbc2e2e72261","clm_ffe6810f4f16b959c6fc8727d30c44136ba5c18fe70b18c44016c41353b03b30"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577","id":"pg_14a5b22d72f356be95150af095b551f5","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/scarmonit-antigravity-jules-orchestration-readme-md-49d26f81817c-0af095b551f5.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f72edac13db859ef8317f3395ac52102"],"title":"Scarmonit/antigravity-jules-orchestration/README.md @ 49d26f81817c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08d8af258fbc47bf85888001c6f96ee1446098cf5d645570565aaab3617343a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture positions Jules API as the inner-loop coding executor (clone, plan, edit, create PRs) with agent.scarmonit.com as an orchestration layer translating events into tasks and managing approval flows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7074de051b24963c255c3e73041ed8c2243e5ca0e879859df1bfb57daf50e46e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system is event-driven, reacting to GitHub labels (jules-auto), comments (@jules plan this), PR review comments, monitoring webhooks, and CI build failures."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d31a662b07743d128b3f4709ee535c3cc08d52fe44c3d8ea5b7a4d815125b4a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Safety design includes approval gates requiring a 'Plan Approved' state before code modification, stricter approval for high-risk infra/auth tasks, and all Jules output delivered via pull requests for human review."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08d8af258fbc47bf85888001c6f96ee1446098cf5d645570565aaab3617343a8","clm_7074de051b24963c255c3e73041ed8c2243e5ca0e879859df1bfb57daf50e46e","clm_d31a662b07743d128b3f4709ee535c3cc08d52fe44c3d8ea5b7a4d815125b4a2"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","created_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577","id":"pg_1d334d82817f56bab515ef5e04704668","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/scarmonit-antigravity-jules-orchestration-docs-reference-architecture--ef5e04704668.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_7262c466551b5dd2b6ddd0b3b2fa2f74"],"title":"Scarmonit/antigravity-jules-orchestration/docs/reference/ARCHITECTURE.md @ 49d26f81817c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:55Z","updated_by_operation":"op_509382cb311b45a59f5db14c40ef5577"}
